---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — FrameCraft"
  description="Terms of Service for using the FrameCraft Video Frame Extractor web application."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-8 space-y-6 font-sans text-sm text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed">
    <div class="border-b border-zinc-850 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-100 tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 font-mono mt-1">Effective Date: September 4, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-amber-400">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing and using FrameCraft, you agree to comply with and be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to these terms, please discontinue use of the tool.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-amber-400">2. Permitted Use</h2>
      <p>
        FrameCraft is provided for lawful personal, commercial, educational, and creative purposes. You retain full copyright and ownership of all video files and extracted image assets processed through the tool. You agree not to use FrameCraft to process content that violates applicable intellectual property or copyright laws.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-amber-400">3. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p>
        FrameCraft is provided on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied. We do not guarantee uninterrupted availability or error-free operation.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
